1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Choosing the version:** v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. Both v2.3.1 and the v2.3.1-rc before it were marked unhealthy.\n- **After:** all regions are on v2.3.0, health checks pass and the error rate is 0.2%.\n- **Incident INC-0001:** it says what failed, which version I rolled back to and why, and the health numbers after the rollback. It also says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before anyone redeploys it.\n\nNo approval was needed, because the policy only covers deploying versions that have never been healthy, and v2.3.0 has been healthy before.", "type": "text"}]}]}